{"name":"Va Va Voom","hex":"#e3b34c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"va-va-voom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Expressing that something is lively, sexy, passionate, or exciting."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Lively excitement or sexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/va-va-voom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Va Va Voom","blocks":[{"text":"\"Va Va Voom\" is a song by rapper Nicki Minaj from the deluxe edition of her second studio album, Pink Friday: Roman Reloaded (2012). It was released on October 23, 2012 by Young Money, Cash Money, and Universal Republic as the sixth and final single from the album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1f/NickiMinaj-VaVaVoom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Va_Va_Voom"},{"title":"Va Va Voom (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Va Va Voom is the debut album by the English indie rock band Cinerama, released in 1998."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fb/Va_Va_Voom_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Va_Va_Voom_(album)"},{"title":"Voom HD Networks","blocks":[{"text":"Voom HD Networks was a suite of 25 original high-definition television channels owned by AMC Networks. At the time, the channels were the largest suite of high-definition channels in the world as part of a 15-year agreement between AMC Networks and Dish Network."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c8/Voom_HD_Networks_logo.svg/330px-Voom_HD_Networks_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voom_HD_Networks"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ee/VVVoomMinaj.jpg/330px-VVVoomMinaj.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x"